00:20:28.978 --> 00:20:30.621
Design Document Excerpt.

263
00:20:31.871 --> 00:20:32.617
Note:

264
00:20:32.897 --> 00:20:37.697
Design Document (excerpt), Pending-Outcome Resolution for UPI Debits.

265
00:20:37.977 --> 00:20:44.036
Context, Credit-leg timeouts during beneficiary-bank incidents leave debited payments unknown.

266
00:20:44.316 --> 00:20:51.228
The current auto-reverse rule caused double payments, and the previous treat as success rule caused TAT breaches.

267
00:20:51.508 --> 00:20:56.735
Decision, A PENDING state with scheduled status checks (30 s to 2 h, jittered).

268
00:20:57.015 --> 00:21:01.836
Resolution from status responses or settlement files, whichever arrives first.

269
00:21:02.116 --> 00:21:08.921
Unknowns are reversed at the next settlement cycle, never later than the TAT deadline minus a safety margin.

270
00:21:09.201 --> 00:21:23.943
Related ADRs, ADR-I03 to 1 append-only journal for hot accounts; ADR-I03 to 2 decimal accrual with single rounding; ADR-I03 to 3 mule scoring with graph features.

271
00:21:25.293 --> 00:21:26.253
Requirements.

272
00:21:26.533 --> 00:21:27.365
R1:

273
00:21:27.645 --> 00:21:32.786
No customer is refunded for a payment that was credited (no double payment from our side).

274
00:21:33.066 --> 00:21:33.898
R2:

275
00:21:34.178 --> 00:21:42.114
Every failed payment is reversed within the TAT (VERIFY current TAT), and at P99 within the same business day.

276
00:21:42.394 --> 00:21:43.247
R3:

277
00:21:43.527 --> 00:21:48.413
Status checks never exceed an agreed rate towards the switch, even after an incident.

278
00:21:48.693 --> 00:21:49.589
R4:

279
00:21:49.869 --> 00:21:53.773
Customers see the PENDING status and an expected resolution time.

280
00:21:55.123 --> 00:21:55.997
R5:

281
00:21:56.277 --> 00:22:01.995
Every PENDING has an audit trail: checks, responses, the settlement record and the final action.

282
00:22:02.275 --> 00:22:03.683
Decisions in detail.

283
00:22:03.963 --> 00:22:06.160
Settlement files are the source of truth.

284
00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:08.168
Status checks shorten the wait.

285
00:22:08.448 --> 00:22:14.784
Reversal is itself idempotent on the transaction reference, and can race with a late credit confirmation.

286
00:22:15.064 --> 00:22:18.755
The state machine guards it: only PENDING can move to REVERSED.

287
00:22:19.035 --> 00:22:24.325
Status-check load is spread with jitter and capped by a token bucket (Ch 39).

288
00:22:25.675 --> 00:22:29.537
TAT dashboards show the oldest PENDING per beneficiary bank.

289
00:22:29.817 --> 00:22:30.841
Consequences.

290
00:22:31.121 --> 00:22:34.491
Some customers wait hours after long incidents (L2:

291
00:22:34.771 --> 00:22:38.483
22,593 more than 1 h).

292
00:22:38.763 --> 00:22:42.091
Messaging and expectation-setting are part of the design.

