00:34:38.161 --> 00:34:44.881
623,328 transfers among 200,000 accounts; hidden:

405
00:34:45.161 --> 00:34:49.449
80 mules and 24 collectors in 8. rings. look-alikes:

406
00:34:49.729 --> 00:34:57.857
3,000 shops, 2,000 salary-then-rent payers, 800 group collectors. rule flagged true bad precision recall.

407
00:34:58.137 --> 00:35:09.572
D1 fan-in: ≥ 15 distinct senders within 2 h 3,482 80 2.3% 76.9%.

408
00:35:09.852 --> 00:35:22.012
D2 pass-through: ≥ 80% of 2-h inflow sent on (P2P) 15,040 81 0.5% 77.9%.

409
00:35:22.292 --> 00:35:37.780
D3 fan-in + pass ≥ 85% to at most 2 receivers + ≥ 15 thousand rupees (same 2 h) 68 67 98.5% 64.4%.

410
00:35:38.060 --> 00:35:49.559
D4 D3 + accounts fed by ≥ 2 D3 accounts (collectors) 93 90 96.8% 86.5%.

411
00:35:49.839 --> 00:35:58.436
D3 finds 67 of 80 mules and 0 collectors; D4 adds 23 of 24 collectors. false positives:

412
00:35:58.716 --> 00:36:00.593
D3 1, D4 3.

413
00:36:03.443 --> 00:36:04.297
Reading it:

414
00:36:04.577 --> 00:36:12.406
Fan-in alone (D1) flags 3,482 accounts, mostly shops, at 2.3% precision.

415
00:36:12.686 --> 00:36:22.499
Pass-through alone (D2) flags 15,040, catching salaried people paying rent and group collectors, at 0.5% precision.

416
00:36:22.779 --> 00:36:24.635
Either would drown investigators.

417
00:36:24.915 --> 00:36:33.577
Combining them in the same 2-hour window (D3) reaches 98.5% precision and finds 67 of 80 mules.

418
00:36:33.857 --> 00:36:38.913
The window requires: many senders;. ≥ 85% forwarded;.

419
00:36:40.263 --> 00:36:44.956
to at most 2 personal accounts;. ≥ 15,000 rupees.

420
00:36:45.236 --> 00:36:50.569
Excluding payments to registered merchants removes group collections, which pay a vendor.

421
00:36:50.849 --> 00:36:58.828
Following the money (D4): accounts fed by ≥ 2 flagged mules add 23 of 24 collectors.

422
00:36:59.108 --> 00:37:04.164
Overall that is 90 of 104 bad accounts, with 3 false positives.

423
00:37:04.444 --> 00:37:07.132
The misses and the design choices were deliberate:

424
00:37:08.482 --> 00:37:12.087
The first version measured pass-through after the last credit of the day.

425
00:37:12.367 --> 00:37:17.103
Ordinary transfers arriving later hid the pattern, and recall was 5%.

426
00:37:17.383 --> 00:37:18.877
Windowed features fixed it.

427
00:37:19.157 --> 00:37:25.237
Counting receivers over the whole day also hid mules, so the receiver count is now taken within the window.

428
00:37:25.517 --> 00:37:27.373
Synthetic data flatters rules.

429
00:37:27.653 --> 00:37:34.799
Real deployments need labelled cases, models, and review before account restrictions (VERIFY legal process).

